#!/usr/bin/env python3
# THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 18 — CHAPTERS 26-28 (LEAN, 2026-09-26): chapter 26's Sifrei rows TYPED, piskaot 297-300 (19 rows — 297 on 26:1-2 ten rows; 298
# HEADLESS inside 26:2 three; 299 HEADLESS inside 26:3 four; 300 on 26:4 two): entering and settling, the first-fruits' species by the two-loaves' analogy, a
# cluster or a grape, fruit not wine, whose soil, the basket a vessel, Shiloh and the eternal house, the priest of your days, no ingratitude, once a year, proselytes
# and slaves and Trans-Jordan excluded, silver trays and willow baskets, the waving, no altar no first-fruits, stolen or unclean. Every row READ WHOLE in both
# files (the whole-row rule); the cuts by ch26_ink.SP_ (the misses collected). Sitting 17's form (ch22_rows_sifrei_222_226.py).
from ch26_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(297, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"NOW IT SHALL BE, WHEN YOU ENTER THE LAND" (26:1) — "IT SHALL BE" MEANS AT ONCE; "WHEN YOU ENTER THE LAND" — DO THE COMMANDMENT OF THIS PASSAGE, FOR BY ITS REWARD YOU ENTER THE LAND. The head row of piska 297 ({SP_(297, 1, "אין", "והיה", "אלא", "מיד")} "\'it shall be\' is only at once"; {SP_(297, 1, "שבשכרה", "תכנס", "לארץ")} "by whose reward you enter the land"): THE TIMING of the first-fruits — no delay after the entry — and THE REWARD FORMULA (the land for the commandment; 296:1\'s and 57:1\'s parallels named by the translator). Fresh.')
srow(297, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHICH THE LORD YOUR GOD GIVES YOU AS AN INHERITANCE, AND YOU POSSESS IT AND DWELL IN IT" — WHAT YOU INHERIT YOU CONQUER. ({SP_(297, 2, "מה", "שתירש", "תכבש")} "what you inherit, you conquer"): the possession by CONQUEST — the first condition of the duty (the land held, not merely entered). Fresh.')
srow(297, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU POSSESS IT AND DWELL IN IT" — AFTER YOU INHERIT, YOU DWELL. ({SP_(297, 3, "משתירש", "תשב")} "after you inherit, dwell"): THE ORDER inherit then settle — the duty waits for the settlement (the compile\'s condition: the first-fruits after the conquest and the division). Fresh.')
srow(297, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL TAKE FROM THE FIRST OF ALL THE FRUIT OF THE GROUND" (26:2) — ARE ALL FRUITS LIABLE TO FIRST-FRUITS? "FROM THE FIRST" — AND NOT ALL THE FIRST. WHICH KIND IS LIABLE? THE COMMUNITY\'S FIRST-FRUITS (LEVITICUS 23:17, THE TWO LOAVES) ARE OF THE SEVEN SPECIES — SO THE INDIVIDUAL\'S; THERE WHEAT AND BARLEY — WHENCE THE OTHER KINDS? "THE FIRST-FRUITS OF YOUR SOIL" (EXODUS 23:19) WIDENED; WIDENED THEN NARROWED — THE FIRST ARGUMENT STANDS: THE SEVEN SPECIES FOR WHICH THE LAND IS PRAISED, "WHEAT, BARLEY, VINE, FIG, POMEGRANATE, OLIVE OIL AND HONEY" (8:8). ({SP_(297, 4, "יכול", "כל", "הפרות", "יהו", "חיבים", "בבכורים")} "could all fruits be liable to first-fruits?"; {SP_(297, 4, "מראשית", "ולא", "כל", "ראשית")} "from the first — and not all the first"; {SP_(297, 4, "משבעת", "המינים")} "of the seven species"; {SP_(297, 4, "חטה", "ושערה", "וגפן", "ותאנה", "ורמון")} "wheat, barley, vine, fig, pomegranate"): THE SPECIES PARAMETER of the first-fruits — the seven of 8:8 by the analogy of the community\'s two loaves (Bikkurim 1:3\'s rule inside the spine; the translator cites 1:10) — the compile\'s parameter for 26:2. REREAD WHOLE (chapter 8, deu_08_ekev).')
srow(297, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"OLIVE" — THIS IS THE OIL-STORING OLIVE (AGURI). ({SP_(297, 5, "זית", "אגורי")} "the aguri olive"): the sixth species narrowed to the superior olive. Fresh.')
srow(297, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HONEY" — THIS IS DATE-HONEY. ({SP_(297, 6, "דבש", "תמרים")} "date honey"): the seventh species the date, not the bee — 8:8\'s honey read as fruit. Fresh.')
srow(297, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"FROM THE FIRST" — EVEN ONE CLUSTER, EVEN ONE GRAPE. ({SP_(297, 7, "אפלו", "אשכול", "אחד")} "even one cluster"; {SP_(297, 7, "גרגיר", "אחד")} "one grape"): NO MEASURE — the first-fruits have no minimum (Peah 1:1\'s "these have no measure" the translator\'s ground). Fresh.')
srow(297, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"FRUIT" — FRUIT YOU BRING AS FIRST-FRUITS; YOU DO NOT BRING WINE OR OIL. ({SP_(297, 8, "ואי", "אתה", "מביא", "יין", "ושמן")} "and you do not bring wine and oil"): THE FORM PARAMETER — the fruit in kind, not its product (Terumot 11:3 beside). Fresh.')
srow(297, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE GROUND" — EXCLUDING SHARECROPPERS, TENANTS, EXTORTIONERS AND ROBBERS, WHO DO NOT BRING, BY "THE FIRST-FRUITS OF YOUR SOIL"; MAY YOU BRING AS LONG AS YOU MAY RECITE? "WHICH YOU BRING FROM YOUR LAND" — AS LONG AS THEY ARE FOUND ON YOUR LAND; MAY YOU RECITE AS LONG AS YOU BRING? "AND YOU SHALL SAY … AND REJOICE" — RECITATION ONLY IN A TIME OF JOY: FROM THE FEAST OF WEEKS TO THE FEAST OF BOOTHS ONE BRINGS AND RECITES, FROM BOOTHS TO CHANUKAH ONE BRINGS AND DOES NOT RECITE; R. JUDAH B. BETHYRA: BRINGS AND RECITES. ({SP_(297, 9, "פרט", "לעריסים", "ולחכורות", "ולסקריקון", "ולגזלן")} "excluding sharecroppers, tenants, extortioners and the robber"; {SP_(297, 9, "אין", "קריאה", "אלא", "בשעת", "שמחה")} "recitation only in a time of joy"; {SP_(297, 9, "מעצרת", "ועד", "החג", "מביא", "וקורא")} "from the Feast of Weeks until the Feast one brings and recites"; {SP_(297, 9, "מהחג", "ועד", "חנכה", "מביא", "ואינו", "קורא")} "from the Feast until Chanukah one brings and does not recite"): THE OWNER and THE CLOCK — the soil his own (Bikkurim 1:2), the bringing while the fruit stands, THE RECITATION\'S SEASON Weeks to Booths, the bringing without recitation to Chanukah (Bikkurim 1:6), the dissent — the compile\'s clock parameters for 26:2-3. Fresh.')
srow(297, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHICH THE LORD YOUR GOD GIVES YOU" — EXCLUDING ONE WHO PLANTS IN HIS OWN AND SINKS A SHOOT INTO ANOTHER\'S OR THE PUBLIC\'S, OR FROM THEM INTO HIS OWN, OR WITHIN HIS OWN WITH A PUBLIC OR PRIVATE PATH BETWEEN — HE DOES NOT BRING; R. JUDAH: HE BRINGS; WHY NOT? "THE FIRST-FRUITS OF YOUR SOIL" — UNTIL ALL THE GROWTH IS FROM YOUR SOIL. ({SP_(297, 10, "פרט", "לנוטע", "בתוך", "שלו", "ומבריך")} "excluding one who plants in his own and sinks a shoot"; {SP_(297, 10, "הרי", "זה", "אינו", "מביא")} "this one does not bring"; {SP_(297, 10, "עד", "שיהו", "כל", "הגדולים", "מאדמתך")} "until all the growth is from your soil"): THE SOIL WHOLE — the shoot crossing a boundary bars the bringing (Bikkurim 1:1-2), R. Judah dissenting; the compile\'s predicate on "your soil". Fresh.')
srow(298, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND PLACE IT IN A BASKET" (26:2) — THIS TEACHES THAT THEY REQUIRE A VESSEL. The head row of the headless piska 298 ({SP_(298, 1, "מלמד", "שטעונים", "כלי")} "teaches that they require a vessel"): THE VESSEL a condition of the rite. Fresh.')
srow(298, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND GO TO THE PLACE WHICH THE LORD YOUR GOD WILL CHOOSE" — THIS IS SHILOH AND THE ETERNAL HOUSE. ({SP_(298, 2, "זה", "שילה", "ובית", "עולמים")} "this is Shiloh and the eternal house"): THE PLACE formula read as two seats in history — Shiloh, then Jerusalem (the chosen-place daemon\'s two settings on the tape). Fresh.')
srow(298, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND COME TO THE PRIEST WHO SHALL BE IN THOSE DAYS" (26:3) — R. YOSE THE GALILEAN: WOULD WE GO TO A PRIEST NOT OF OUR DAYS? A PRIEST FIT AND ESTABLISHED IN THOSE DAYS; A KINSMAN WHO BECAME DISTANT — FIT; "SAY NOT THE FORMER DAYS WERE BETTER" (ECCLESIASTES 7:10). ({SP_(298, 3, "וכי", "עלתה", "על", "דעתנו", "כהן", "שאינו", "בימיך")} "would it enter our mind — a priest not of your days?"; {SP_(298, 3, "היה", "קרוב", "ונתרחק", "כשר")} "he was near and became distant — fit"): THE PRIEST OF YOUR DAYS — the officiant\'s standing his own generation\'s (153:2 and 190:3 the same teaching at the judge and the elders); the compile\'s officiant parameter. Fresh.')
srow(299, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL SAY TO HIM" (26:3) — AND NOT UNGRATEFUL. The head row of the headless piska 299 ({SP_(299, 1, "ולא", "כפוי", "טובה")} "and not one who denies the good"): THE DECLARATION AS THANKS — the saying a duty against ingratitude. Fresh.')
srow(299, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"I DECLARE THIS DAY TO THE LORD YOUR GOD THAT I HAVE COME" — ONCE A YEAR YOU RECITE, NOT TWICE. ({SP_(299, 2, "פעם", "אחת", "אתה", "קורא", "בשנה")} "once a year you recite"): THE RECITATION\'S COUNT — one per year (Tosefta Bikkurim 1:4 beside); the compile\'s clock. Fresh.')
srow(299, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"THAT I HAVE COME TO THE LAND WHICH THE LORD SWORE TO OUR FATHERS" — EXCLUDING PROSELYTES. ({SP_(299, 3, "פרט", "לגרים")} "excluding proselytes"): THE RECITER\'S LINEAGE — the fathers\' oath the proselyte cannot claim (Bikkurim 1:4; 301:37 the confessors); the compile\'s reciter parameter. Fresh.')
srow(299, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO GIVE TO US" — EXCLUDING SLAVES; R. SIMEON: EXCLUDING TRANS-JORDAN, WHICH YOU TOOK FOR YOURSELVES. ({SP_(299, 4, "פרט", "לעבדים")} "excluding slaves"; {SP_(299, 4, "פרט", "לעבר", "הירדן", "שנטלתו", "מעצמך")} "excluding the other side of the Jordan, which you took of yourself"): the slave without land; TRANS-JORDAN not the sworn land — R. Simeon\'s exclusion (301:27 R. Yose\'s by milk and honey; Bikkurim 1:10) — the compile\'s territory parameter. Fresh.')
srow(300, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE PRIEST SHALL TAKE THE BASKET FROM YOUR HAND" (26:4) — HENCE: THE RICH BRING THEIR FIRST-FRUITS IN TRAYS OF SILVER AND GOLD, THE POOR IN BASKETS OF PEELED WILLOW, AND THE BASKETS AND THE FIRST-FRUITS ARE GIVEN TO THE PRIESTS, TO INCREASE THE PRIESTS\' GIFTS. The head row of piska 300 ({SP_(300, 1, "העשירים", "מביאים", "בכוריהם", "בקלתות", "של", "כסף")} "the rich bring their first-fruits in trays of silver"; {SP_(300, 1, "בסלי", "נצרים", "של", "ערבה", "קלופה")} "in baskets of peeled willow twigs"): THE BASKET given with the fruit — the poor man\'s basket the priest\'s (Bikkurim 3:8 inside the spine). Fresh.')
srow(300, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"FROM YOUR HAND" — THEY REQUIRE WAVING: R. ELIEZER B. JACOB; "AND SET IT BEFORE THE ALTAR OF THE LORD YOUR GOD" — WHILE YOU HAVE AN ALTAR YOU HAVE FIRST-FRUITS, WITHOUT AN ALTAR NO FIRST-FRUITS; "AND SET IT" — HENCE: STOLEN OR LOST, HE IS LIABLE FOR THEM; MADE UNCLEAN IN THE COURT, HE SCATTERS THEM AND DOES NOT RECITE. ({SP_(300, 2, "מלמד", "שטעונים", "תנופה")} "teaches that they require waving"; {SP_(300, 2, "כל", "זמן", "שיש", "לך", "מזבח", "יש", "לך", "בכורים")} "whenever you have an altar you have first-fruits"; {SP_(300, 2, "נגנבו", "או", "אבדו", "חיב", "באחריותם")} "stolen or lost — liable for them"; {SP_(300, 2, "נטמאו", "בעזרה", "נופץ", "ואינו", "קורא")} "made unclean in the court — he scatters and does not recite"): THE WAVING (Bikkurim 2:4), THE ALTAR THE CONDITION (Tosefta Shekalim 3:24 — no Temple, no first-fruits: the daemon\'s own guard), THE LIABILITY until the setting, THE UNCLEAN scattered without the recitation (Bikkurim 1:8). Fresh.')
